[Result "*"]
[FEN "1Q6/5p2/6k1/1P4p1/1q5p/7P/6P1/7K b - - 0 1"]

 { Black is on the verge of losing, but by exposing the enemy king to checks he can still save a draw. } 1... { -KEY- } f5 $1 { Heading for f4 in order to create checking possibilities on g3-e1 before White prevails on the opposite flank. } ( { Less convincing is } 1... g4 $6 2. hxg4 h3 ( { not } 2... Qxg4 $4 3. Qg8 ) 
3. Qg8 Kf6 4. Qd8 Kg7 5. Qd3 hxg2 6. Kxg2 { and White keeps some chances for a win. } ) 
2. b6 f4 $1 ( { Simplest; though } 2... g4 { also works - Gufeld; e.g. } 3. hxg4 fxg4 4. b7 Qe1 5. Kh2 Qe6 $1 { preparing 6...g3+. } ) 
 ( 2... Qe1 3. Kh2 f4 { is another possible move order, and actually 1...Qe1+ also worked on the previous move. Still, it seems more logical to keep this check in the pocket so that White's queen remains tied to the b-pawn. } ) 
3. b7 ( { Or } 3. Kh2 $5 Qb3 $1 { eyeing the g3-square. } ) 
Qe1+ 4. Kh2 Qg3+ { Draw. } 
